# Big Idea 1: Humans Shape AI Outputs

One of the first major ideas students encounter in **Thinking Critically About AI** is that AI systems do not generate outputs randomly. Instead, outputs are shaped by prompts and the examples and training data AI learns from.

## What Students Learn

<div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:14px; margin:25px 0px;">

  <div style="background-color:#F5F7F8; padding:18px; border-radius:10px; width:32%; text-align:center;">
    <p style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; margin-top:0;">
      Prompts Shape Outputs
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; margin-bottom:0;">
      Students learn that the details, context, and goals included in prompts directly influence what AI generates.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="background-color:#F5F7F8; padding:18px; border-radius:10px; width:32%; text-align:center;">
    <p style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; margin-top:0;">
      AI Predicts Patterns
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; margin-bottom:0;">
      Students investigate how AI systems generate outputs by predicting patterns from training data.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="background-color:#F5F7F8; padding:18px; border-radius:10px; width:32%; text-align:center;">
    <p style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; margin-top:0;">
      Assumptions Become Defaults
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; margin-bottom:0;">
      Students explore how repeated patterns in training data can create biased or incomplete outputs.
    </p>
  </div>

</div>

A major instructional goal of this section of the unit is helping students recognize that AI outputs are not neutral or objective.

## Across the Unit


Throughout the first half of the unit, students begin moving away from thinking about AI as “magic” or “thinking like a human” and toward understanding that AI systems predict patterns based on what they have seen before.

* **Lesson 1** introduces prompting and systematic testing through AI image generation
* **Lesson 3** explores how large language models predict patterns in text
* **Lesson 4** investigates how AI-generated images reflect assumptions embedded in training data
* **Lesson 5** helps students understand how prompts containing context and goals shape chatbot behavior

Across these lessons, students gradually build a more accurate mental model of how AI systems generate outputs and why those systems can sometimes produce biased, incomplete, or unexpected results.

